# Single page notification button

The publishing notification control subscribes a person to updates about one page and exposes an unsubscribe state. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/single-page-notification-button/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

For household notifications, route to a real automation or notification preference owned by Home Assistant. Name the event and destination, such as an existing mobile notification channel. Documentation release alerts can link to an actual repository subscription facility, with its external account context clear.

## Structure and behaviour

A subscription has distinct loading, subscribed, unsubscribed and failed states. Only switch the displayed state after the responsible service confirms the result. A bell icon is decorative when visible text names the action. Allow the person to stop the same subscription from the same context.

## Home Assistant boundary

This theme adds no email subscription backend and does not request a GOV.UK account. The examples illustrate copy and local status messages only. They must not report that a household automation was enabled or an address subscribed.

